Stock-based compensation, a non-cash compensation expense rather than a cash use, was $6.39B [f_648b86ee1ddb] in the latest annual trailing-12-month window and equaled 6.22% [f_7bd75f43d9ff] of operating cash flow. Across the three annual periods, its operating-cash-flow share declined consistently from 12.6% [f_bba0ee94c00e] to 7.39% [f_148f1b24daa3] and 6.22% [f_7bd75f43d9ff]. [table: sbc_share]", "title": "NVIDIA operating cash flow allocation and stock-based compensation"}, "coverage": {"done": 4, "asked": 4, "refused": 0, "not_done": 0}}

{"brief": {"caveats": ["The margin method returned annual spacing over 2021-12-31 through 2025-12-31, not the requested latest twelve fiscal quarters.", "The latest filing passage supports only the Q1 2026 versus Q1 2025 source assessment; it does not establish the driver across all twelve requested quarters.", "Product-mix effects were not separately quantified in the filed lines returned."], "findings": [{"want": 3, "facts": ["f_43993fc373ff"], "finding": "The latest filing says gross margin as a percent of revenue was 81.9% in Q1 2026 versus 82.5% in Q1 2025 and attributes the 0.6-point decline primarily to lower realized prices [f_43993fc373ff]. This supports pricing—not favorable costs—as the immediate gross-margin explanation, while the available evidence does not isolate product mix."}], "not_done": [{"why": "The registry could not derive Lilly gross or operating margin because the required gross-profit and operating-income lines are absent, and the requested 12-quarter read resolved only to five annual periods rather than quarters.", "want": 1, "boundary": "f_538290d24e31"}, {"why": "The quarterly gross-to-operating margin gap could not be calculated because both source-margin series were refused, beginning with absent gross profit.", "want": 2, "boundary": "f_2dca38e17336"}, {"why": "Merck is unprepared on the desk and therefore remains explicitly unmeasured; Lilly's gross and operating series also could not be derived, so no matched 12-quarter comparison can be concluded now.", "want": 4, "boundary": "f_0967f298f916"}], "follow_ups": ["Prepare MRK with a readiness task, then rerun matched-quarter margins and comparison gaps.", "Map Lilly's reported gross-margin and expense lines from filing tables if a full filing-prose reconstruction of twelve quarters is required."]}, "report": {"text": "The requested twelve-quarter margin panel was not computable from registry methods. Lilly gross margin was refused because no gross_profit line was available [f_538290d24e31], operating margin was likewise unavailable [f_125705bff41a], and the gross-minus-operating gap consequently failed [f_2dca38e17336]. The only computed margin series was net margin, but it had annual spacing over 2021-12-31 through 2025-12-31—not twelve fiscal quarters—so it does not settle line 1.

For source attribution, Lilly's latest 10-Q states: "Gross margin as a percent of revenue decreased 0.6 percentage points for the three months ended March 31, 2026, primarily driven by lower realized prices" [f_43993fc373ff]. The same passage reports gross margin as a percent of revenue of 81.9% for Q1 2026 and 82.5% for Q1 2025 [f_43993fc373ff]. This points to adverse realized pricing rather than favorable cost behavior for the latest year-over-year gross-margin movement; product mix was not isolated by the returned evidence.

Merck was unknown to the desk, so its gross, operating, and net margins are unmeasured [f_0967f298f916] [f_9b286ba392a9] [f_cd7f568bed94]. No Lilly-minus-Merck matching-quarter gaps can be stated, and no comparative conclusion is supported yet.", "title": "Lilly profitability and Merck benchmark — evidence record"}, "coverage": {"done": 1, "asked": 4, "refused": 0, "not_done": 3}}

{"brief": {"caveats": ["Gross and operating margin series were not derivable because filed gross-profit and operating-income period lines were unavailable; no quarterly margin direction was inferred.", "“Operating profitability” is read through Item 7’s gross-margin and operating-expense explanations because the filing passage does not separately state an operating-margin bridge.", "Prior Item 7 was not needed to determine the scope of the latest filing; the latest Item 7 explicitly refers the 2024-versus-2023 discussion elsewhere."], "findings": [{"want": 3, "facts": ["f_6a9b3775da31", "f_0f8db89bef75"], "finding": "The latest Item 7 explains only the 2025-versus-2024 annual comparison and directs readers to the prior 10-K’s Item 7 for 2024-versus-2023; it does not explain a twelve-quarter direction. The desk could derive only an annual net-margin series: 19.7% [f_0f8db89bef75@2021-12-31], 21.9% [f_0f8db89bef75@2022-12-31], 15.4% [f_0f8db89bef75@2023-12-31], 23.5% [f_0f8db89bef75@2024-12-31], and 31.7% [f_0f8db89bef75@2025-12-31]. [f_6a9b3775da31]"}], "not_done": [], "follow_ups": ["If needed, retrieve the 2024 10-K Item 7 to extend management’s annual explanations through 2024 versus 2023."]}, "report": {"text": "Lilly’s latest Item 7 frames the gross-margin change as a favorable product-mix and production-cost story, partly offset by lower realized pricing. It says net income increased primarily because of higher gross margin, partly offset by higher marketing, selling and administrative expense and R&D expense. The expense explanations are specific: R&D rose with continued early- and late-stage portfolio investment, while marketing expense rose with promotional support for ongoing and planned launches. [f_e0d56452af88] [f_2861e6bc4e8e]

The filing preserves important qualifications. Product mix and improved cost of production were the primary favorable gross-margin drivers; lower realized prices were only a partial offset. Acquired IPR&D charges were associated mainly with Scorpion’s STX-478 program and SiteOne in 2025 versus Morphic in 2024. The effective-tax-rate increase was attributed primarily to unfavorable jurisdictional earnings mix and U.S. tax-law changes; non-deductible acquired IPR&D adversely affected both years, but more strongly in 2024. [f_2861e6bc4e8e]

The latest Item 7 explains only 2025 against 2024 and directs the reader to the prior annual report for 2024 against 2023; it does not explain a twelve-quarter direction. [f_6a9b3775da31] The desk could derive only an annual net-margin series spanning 2021–2025: 19.7% [f_0f8db89bef75@2021-12-31], 21.9% [f_0f8db89bef75@2022-12-31], 15.4% [f_0f8db89bef75@2023-12-31], 23.5% [f_0f8db89bef75@2024-12-31], and 31.7% [f_0f8db89bef75@2025-12-31]. Gross and operating margin series were unavailable because the required filed period lines were absent, so no quarterly gross- or operating-margin direction is claimed.", "title": "LLY profitability attribution — latest Item 7"}, "coverage": {"done": 1, "asked": 3, "refused": 0, "not_done": 0}, "problems": [{"fix": "line 1 of the task has no finding and no not_done entry: answer it, or say what stopped you and point at the boundary", "line": "Read the latest Item 7 and report what Lilly attributes changes in gross, operating, and net profitability to.", "want": 1, "where": "coverage", "reason": "uncovered_want"}, {"fix": "line 2 of the task has no finding and no not_done entry: answer it, or say what stopped you and point at the boundary", "line": "Separate the filing's explanations into pricing, product mix, and cost effects, preserving any qualifications.", "want": 2, "where": "coverage", "reason": "uncovered_want"}]}

{"brief": {"caveats": ["Product amounts are presented for both three- and six-month periods because the verified filing passage provides both; column order is preserved exactly.", "The geographic extract uses the fully visible six-month table because the three-month passage was truncated before Rest of Asia Pacific and total.", "No arithmetic was performed outside the desk ledger, and refused calculations were not reported."], "findings": [{"want": 1, "facts": ["f_727421a3e89f"], "finding": "The latest 10-Q says, “The following table shows disaggregated net sales, as well as the portion of total net sales that was previously deferred, for the three- and six-month periods ended March 28, 2026 and March 29, 2025 (in millions)” and reports, in column order, iPhone “$56,994 $46,841 $142,263 $115,979,” Mac “8,399 7,949 16,785 16,936,” iPad “6,914 6,402 15,509 14,490,” Wearables, Home and Accessories “7,901 7,522 19,394 19,269,” Services “30,976 26,645 60,989 52,985,” and Total net sales “$111,184 $95,359 $254,940 $219,659.” [f_727421a3e89f]"}, {"want": 2, "facts": ["f_7cc5adfb098f"], "finding": "For the six months ended March 28, 2026, the filing presents columns for Americas, Europe, Greater China, Japan, Rest of Asia Pacific, Corporate and Total, with net sales of “$103,622 $66,201 $46,023 $17,814 $21,280 $— $254,940” (millions), respectively. [f_7cc5adfb098f]"}], "not_done": [{"why": "The filing quotes category and total revenue, but filing-prose values are not programmable facts, and the attempted share-ranking program was refused; therefore no verified computed shares are available.", "want": 3, "boundary": "f_56075504ee02"}], "follow_ups": ["If the lead requires three-month geography specifically, obtain a complete verified filing passage containing the entire row.", "If the desk adds programmable filing-prose table values, rerun product and geographic shares and rankings."]}, "report": {"text": "Apple’s latest indexed filing is Q2 2026 Form 10-Q accession 00003201